From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:01:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: sw43402: store DSC bits_per_pixel in 1/16th units

drm_dsc_config.bits_per_pixel is defined in 1/16th-of-a-bit units, but the
driver stored a plain integer 8 and carried a local <<4 shim around
drm_dsc_pps_payload_pack() to compensate, because the msm host code it was
written against consumed the field as a plain integer.

msm now consumes the field in its defined units and rejects the old value
outright: dsi_update_dsc_timing() reads 8 as 0.5 bpp and
msm_dsi_host_power_on() fails with "DSI does not support fractional
bits_per_pixel", so the panel never initializes. Store 8 << 4 and drop the
shim.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c | 21 ++-------------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
index 3a96c6b6be03..66551d919785 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
@@ -169,24 +169,7 @@ static int lg_panel_enable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (ctx->dsi->dsc) {
-		/*
-		 * drm_dsc_pps_payload_pack() takes bits_per_pixel in 1/16ths
-		 * ("bits_per_pixel << 4", see struct drm_dsc_config), but the
-		 * msm code around it uses a plain integer: dsi_populate_dsc_params()
-		 * computes slice_chunk_size = slice_width * bits_per_pixel / 8
-		 * = 720, and dpu_hw_dsc_config() converts 8 into the 6.4-format
-		 * 128 the DSC_ENC register wants. This tree predates the
-		 * conversion upstream did, so only the PPS needs fixing up --
-		 * doing it here rather than changing the value everyone else
-		 * reads.
-		 *
-		 * Without this the panel is told to decode 0.5 bpp while the
-		 * DPU compresses at 8, and the screen is full-frame noise.
-		 */
-		struct drm_dsc_config pps_cfg = *ctx->dsi->dsc;
-
-		pps_cfg.bits_per_pixel <<= 4;
-		drm_dsc_pps_payload_pack(&pps, &pps_cfg);
+		drm_dsc_pps_payload_pack(&pps, ctx->dsi->dsc);
 
 		ret = mipi_dsi_picture_parameter_set(ctx->dsi, &pps);
 		if (ret < 0) {
@@ -495,7 +478,7 @@ static int lg_sw43402_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	dsc->slice_width = 720;
 	dsc->slice_count = 1;
 	dsc->bits_per_component = 8;
-	dsc->bits_per_pixel = 8;
+	dsc->bits_per_pixel = 8 << 4; /* 1/16th units, 8.0 bpp; 6.18 msm rejects fractional */
 	dsc->block_pred_enable = true;
 
 	/*
